# Served by Workers Static Assets from the UniBooks server Worker
# (server/wrangler.jsonc "assets"), which reads this file as Pages did. These
# rules apply to static assets only: the Worker's own responses (/api/v1,
# /api/chat, /api/cover) set their own headers. /<region>/book is the region's
# app shell fetched through env.ASSETS, so it carries these headers too.
#
# The app, the API (/api/v1) and chat (/api/chat, over wss) are one origin, so connect-src
# needs no deployment-specific host: 'self' plus the third parties listed
# below. The one origin a static file cannot know is the R2 public media
# domain, so what is committed here is a Report-Only policy whose img-src
# falls back to https:. After `ng build`, `node scripts/set-env.js --headers`
# (part of `npm run build`) rewrites the CSP in the *built* copy of this file:
#
#   R2_PUBLIC_URL   the R2 public domain -> img-src, replacing https:
#
# R2_PUBLIC_URL is read from server/wrangler.jsonc "vars" (one source for both
# halves). With it set, NG_APP_CSP_ENFORCE=1 (production.env) promotes the
# policy to an enforcing Content-Security-Policy; without it the policy stays
# Report-Only. Before enforcing, walk a real pass of the app with the console
# open: there is no report-uri, and the flows worth checking are Google
# sign-in, photo upload, chat, and a book page.
#
# Two CSP headers ship, and that is deliberate. The enforcing one carries only
# directives that cost nothing to turn on here — the app has no <object>, no
# cross-origin <form action>, its <base> is this origin, and X-Frame-Options
# already says what frame-ancestors says — so they need no verification pass
# and no opt-in. Without that, a deployment that never sets the flag would run
# with a policy that only ever watches. The Report-Only one carries the full
# policy, including the directives that would take the site down if they were
# wrong. NG_APP_CSP_ENFORCE=1 merges them into a single enforcing header.
#
# What the policy allows and why:
#   script-src   GSI (accounts.google.com) and GA (googletagmanager.com) are
#                injected at runtime. Cloudflare Web Analytics
#                (static.cloudflareinsights.com) is injected into every HTML
#                response at the edge; it reports to this origin's /cdn-cgi/rum,
#                which 'self' in connect-src covers. Its origin rather than
#                beacon.min.js: the file redirects to a versioned path.
#                'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets the barcode
#                scanner compile /zxing/zxing_reader.wasm on browsers without a
#                native BarcodeDetector (iOS); it allows WebAssembly only, not
#                eval().
#                No inline script exists to allow: the pre-paint theme snippet is
#                /theme-init.js, and angular.json turns off inlineCritical,
#                whose <link media="print" onload="this.media='all'"> was an
#                inline event handler.
#   'unsafe-inline' in style-src: Angular writes component styles into <style>
#                tags. Removing it needs build-side nonces, not a header edit.
#   accounts.google.com/gsi/style in style-src: GSI loads its button and
#                One Tap stylesheet from there.
#   fonts.*      the Noto family is loaded from Google Fonts in index.html.
#   img-src      book covers come through this origin's /api/cover proxy;
#                listing photos and avatars come from the R2 domain, Google
#                account avatars from lh3.googleusercontent.com, and GA4's
#                pixels from *.google-analytics.com / *.googletagmanager.com.
#   connect-src  this origin: the API, chat over wss, photo uploads. Then
#                Google sign-in, the admin import's CycleUni lists on GitHub,
#                Firebase push registration, GA4 hits and Sentry reports.
#   frame-src    GSI renders its button and One Tap in an iframe.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://accounts.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/ https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: https://lh3.googleusercontent.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CycleUni/ https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://o4512117291876352.ingest.us.sentry.io; frame-src https://accounts.google.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'

# The admin console previews ad images pasted as foreign https URLs, which the
# site-wide img-src (own media host only) would block. These rules match on the
# URL (a placeholder for the region, since a rule may hold only one splat), so the console's pages get a CSP whose only difference is img-src https:.
# Rules merge and two CSP headers both apply, so the site-wide ones are detached
# first. A browser that navigates into the console from a public page keeps the
# CSP of the page it loaded (client-side routing fetches no new HTML): reload the
# console once and it takes effect. scripts/set-env.js keeps these rules in step
# with the site-wide policy.
/:region/admin
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  ! Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://accounts.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/ https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CycleUni/ https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://o4512117291876352.ingest.us.sentry.io; frame-src https://accounts.google.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'

/:region/admin/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  ! Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://accounts.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/ https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CycleUni/ https://fcmregistrations.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://o4512117291876352.ingest.us.sentry.io; frame-src https://accounts.google.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'

# A year-long cache only for the files whose names carry a content hash.
# It used to sit on /* above, and every rule's headers apply to a matching
# request, so each SPA route (/tw/search, /tw/book, ...) was served as
# index.html with a year-long max-age. A browser holding such a copy after a
# deploy asked for chunks that no longer exist, got index.html back through
# the SPA fallback, and failed with "Expected a JavaScript module script but the
# server responded with text/html". Routes now get the platform's default
# revalidating cache; / and /index.html below say so explicitly.
#
# The same still holds for a hashed name a deployment does not have (yet, at
# that edge, or any more): the SPA fallback (not_found_handling
# single-page-application) answers it with index.html, and these rules, which
# match on the URL alone, stamp that HTML with the year-long cache. Static
# assets cannot tell the two apart without running the Worker first, which
# would bill every asset request, so the browser repairs it instead:
# public/asset-recovery.js refetches a bundle that failed this way and reloads.
/main-*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/polyfills-*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/chunk-*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/styles-*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/ngsw.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/ngsw-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/theme-init.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/asset-recovery.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/safety-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/worker-basic.min.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

/apple-touch-icon-precomposed.png
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache
